# Dotfiles

Personal configuration files managed with [Dotbot](https://github.com/anishathalye/dotbot).

## Quick Start (Recommended)

On a new machine, run:

```bash
bash <(curl -s https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gameforce/dotfiles/master/bootstrap.sh)
```

Or the classic way:

```bash
git clone --recursive git@github.com:gameforce/dotfiles.git ~/.dotfiles
cd ~/.dotfiles
./bootstrap.sh
```

The bootstrap script will:

- Install required packages (`zsh`, `git`, `vim`, `pipx`, `keychain`, etc.)
- Clone/update this repository
- Install/update Dotbot via `pipx`
- Create the necessary symlinks
- Set `zsh` as the default shell

After it finishes, log out and log back in (or run `exec zsh`).

## Manual Installation

If you prefer to do it step by step:

```bash
git clone --recursive git@github.com:gameforce/dotfiles.git ~/.dotfiles
cd ~/.dotfiles
pipx install dotbot
dotbot -d ~/.dotfiles -c install.conf.yaml
chsh -s $(which zsh)
```

## Updating

```bash
cd ~/.dotfiles
git pull
./bootstrap.sh
```

## Structure

| Path | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `shell/` | zsh configuration, aliases, functions, environment |
| `git/` | Git configuration |
| `vim/` | Vim configuration |
| `bin/` | Custom scripts |
| `bootstrap.sh` | One-command installer |
| `install.conf.yaml` | Dotbot configuration |

## Notes

- Uses **Antigen** + **Powerlevel10k**
- SSH key recommended: `~/.ssh/id_ed25519_github`
- `keychain` is used to manage SSH keys
